{"caption":"On a flat white surface, a left hand grips a reflective metallic spherical puzzle ball marked by a seam, while a loose scatter of small metallic jigsaw pieces lies in the center. A right hand, palm up, holds several of the same pieces and lets them slip off one after another onto the central pile, thinning the handful until a single piece rests on the open palm.

The right hand then pinches that last piece between its fingers, repositions it briefly over the scatter, and drops it onto the pile. With the handful now empty, the right hand withdraws out of the top-right of the frame and is gone, leaving only the left hand and the sphere. The central scatter of metallic pieces sits still, slightly enlarged by the recent additions.

The left hand keeps its grip on the sphere but slowly turns it, tilting the seam across the polished surface. As the ball rotates, the surface reveals metallic puzzle pieces already adhered to it together with empty gaps where pieces are missing. Room and hand reflections shift across the chrome as it turns. The sphere stays in roughly the same left-side position throughout.","length_note":""}
